# 1. Markdown Frontmatter — Add `navTitle`

Every documentation page following the naming convention:

`<name>.<lang>.md`

must support a `navTitle` frontmatter property.

Example:

```yaml
---
title: "Introduction to Feluqa"
navTitle: "Introduction"
description: "An introduction to the Feluqa framework."
date: 2026-10-29
lastmod: 2026-10-29
weight: 1
status: "Exploring"
tags: [feluqa, introduction, rust]
draft: false
lang: en
---
```

## Expected behavior

- `title` represents the full document title.
- `navTitle` represents the shorter navigation title.
- Sidebar generation must use `navTitle` when available.
- Navigation labels must fall back to `title` when `navTitle` is missing.
- If both are missing, derive a readable title from the filename.
- The document's actual H1, browser title, and metadata should continue using the appropriate full document title.
- `navTitle` must not unintentionally override SEO titles.
- Navigation labels must respect the current language.
- Existing Markdown files without `navTitle` must continue working.

**IMPORTANT:** Do not require manual navigation configuration for each page. The discovery system must extract this information automatically.

